{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And one who strikes his father or his mother — he shall surely be put to death.</b> A striking that entails a wound from which blood emerges, in the manner of what is written (I Kings 20:37): ״ויכהו האיש הכה ופצוע״ — 'and the man struck him, striking and wounding' — and the intent is his father or his mother. And similarly (Deuteronomy 17:3): ״ויעבד אלהים אחרים וישתחו להם ולשמש או לירח וגו׳״ — 'and served other gods and bowed to them, to the sun or to the moon, etc.' — he does not bow to them together but to the sun or to the moon or to any host of the heavens. And this death is death by strangulation, as our Rabbis of blessed memory explained to us: death mentioned in the Torah without specification is death by strangulation."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:02:24.623636534Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}